  recipeId: robotics
  concept: 'Authored objective: Commission and home all six axes.

    Authored requirement:
    Precharge the shared link, prove separate STO channels, measure six encoder references
    and home.

    General teaching principle: Motion validation must consider correct
    reference, feedback, interlocks and authored limits before declaring a movement
    safe or accurate.

    Only fresh, authoritative game evidence can establish
    that this objective is complete.'
  analogy: A coordinated team needs agreement on position and timing before everyone
    moves.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: Motion feedback and a command signal are not interchangeable evidence
    of successful positioning.
  baseline: "Before working on \u2018Commission and home all six axes\u2019, which
    component, reference or condition mentioned in the authored requirement should
    you inspect first? Explain your reasoning."
  prediction: "For \u2018Commission and home all six axes\u2019, what result or observation
    would you expect if the required setup is correct? Distinguish a predicted result
    from a measured result."
  practice: "In Level 120, perform the objective \u2018Commission and home all six
    axes\u2019 in the actual game laboratory. Compare fresh evidence against: Precharge
    the shared link, prove separate STO channels, measure six encoder references
    and home.\nThe mission evaluator decides completion; this tutorial does not grade
    your answer."
